  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "slug": "do-chua",
      "term": "Do Chua",
      "definition": "Vietnamese pickled carrot and daikon, the signature pickle in banh mi. Made quickly with rice vinegar and sugar, it provides sharp crunch that cuts through the rich pork and pate."
    },
    {
      "slug": "banh-mi-pate",
      "term": "Pate",
      "definition": "The pate spread in a banh mi provides rich, fatty savouriness to balance the pickles and herbs. Chicken liver pate is traditional. Any smooth pate works."
    },
    {
      "slug": "char-grilling",
      "term": "Char-Grilling",
      "definition": "Cooking meat on a very hot ridged griddle pan to create charred stripes and a slightly crisp exterior. For banh mi pork, the char adds smoky flavour that complements the pickles."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A banh mi is built on contrasts: hot pork against cold pickles, rich pate against sharp vinegar, soft crumb against crispy crust. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "do-chua"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "do chua"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " pickled carrot is the pivot of the whole thing. Make it first and let it sit for at least an hour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "banh-mi-pate"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "pate"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is essential. Without it, the sandwich misses a layer of richness. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "char-grilling"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Char-grill"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " the pork slices on a very hot griddle until each piece has dark stripes and is cooked through but still juicy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
